From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:00:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 168/194] hjviewer: the privacy window's helper is started by
 its full path, not guessed from a command line

HJViewer's "hide the screen when connecting" turns privacy mode on, and
on Windows 10 2004 and later (and with the Magnifier way before it) that
starts RuntimeBroker_rustdesk.exe from the install folder in the user's
session. CreateProcessAsUserW got no application name and the unquoted
path as its command line, so Windows took each prefix that ends at a
space as a candidate program. Our default install folder is under
"C:\Program Files", so the first candidate was C:\Program: on a PC where
a file of that name exists, Windows loaded that file (error 193 when it
is no program, and any program a local administrator's leftover put
there otherwise) and the screen was not hidden. The helper's path now
goes in as the application name, and the command line is the same path
in quotes, held in a buffer the call may write to as its LPWSTR
parameter says.

Backported from rustdesk/rustdesk 59f2953c94b8373f124dc38d4fd0635098f7c5cd (fix(windows): name the privacy window executable explicitly (#16711))
Upstream's diff applies unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/privacy_mode/win_topmost_window.rs | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/privacy_mode/win_topmost_window.rs b/src/privacy_mode/win_topmost_window.rs
index b30db5f..c8f865e 100644
--- a/src/privacy_mode/win_topmost_window.rs
+++ b/src/privacy_mode/win_topmost_window.rs
@@ -226,7 +226,14 @@ impl PrivacyModeImpl {
             .to_string();
 
         unsafe {
-            let cmd_utf16: Vec<u16> = cmdline.encode_utf16().chain(Some(0).into_iter()).collect();
+            // The path goes in as `lpApplicationName` too: given only a command line, Windows
+            // treats every whitespace-delimited prefix as a candidate image, and the default
+            // install path contains a space.
+            let app_utf16: Vec<u16> = cmdline.encode_utf16().chain(Some(0).into_iter()).collect();
+            let mut cmd_utf16: Vec<u16> = format!("\"{cmdline}\"")
+                .encode_utf16()
+                .chain(Some(0).into_iter())
+                .collect();
 
             let mut start_info = STARTUPINFOW {
                 cb: 0,
@@ -263,8 +270,8 @@ impl PrivacyModeImpl {
 
             let create_res = CreateProcessAsUserW(
                 token,
-                NULL as _,
-                cmd_utf16.as_ptr() as _,
+                app_utf16.as_ptr() as _,
+                cmd_utf16.as_mut_ptr() as _,
                 NULL as _,
                 NULL as _,
                 FALSE,
